{"type":"data","nodes":[null,{"type":"data","data":[{"nav":1},[2,34,135],{"label":3,"items":4},"Start",[5,18],{"title":6,"path":7,"headings":8},"Installation","/docs/installation",[9,12,15],{"id":10,"text":11},"what-you-need","What you need",{"id":13,"text":14},"get-the-template","Get the template",{"id":16,"text":17},"make-a-site","Make a site",{"title":19,"path":20,"headings":21},"Quick start","/docs/quick-start",[22,25,28,31],{"id":23,"text":24},"1-make-the-site","1. Make the site",{"id":26,"text":27},"2-fill-in-the-config","2. Fill in the config",{"id":29,"text":30},"3-write-the-docs","3. Write the docs",{"id":32,"text":33},"4-publish","4. Publish",{"label":35,"items":36},"Guide",[37,53,78,90,103,119],{"title":38,"path":39,"headings":40},"Configuration","/docs/configuration",[41,44,47,50],{"id":42,"text":43},"fields","Fields",{"id":45,"text":46},"colours","Colours",{"id":48,"text":49},"sections","Sections",{"id":51,"text":52},"the-hero","The hero",{"title":54,"path":55,"headings":56},"Writing docs","/docs/writing-docs",[57,60,63,66,69,72,75],{"id":58,"text":59},"file-names","File names",{"id":61,"text":62},"front-matter","Front matter",{"id":64,"text":65},"the-lead","The lead",{"id":67,"text":68},"headings","Headings",{"id":70,"text":71},"code","Code",{"id":73,"text":74},"links","Links",{"id":76,"text":77},"good-docs-pages","Good docs pages",{"title":79,"path":80,"headings":81},"Changelog","/docs/changelog",[82,83,84,87],{"id":58,"text":59},{"id":61,"text":62},{"id":85,"text":86},"writing-an-entry","Writing an entry",{"id":88,"text":89},"what-the-site-makes-from-it","What the site makes from it",{"title":91,"path":92,"headings":93},"Custom hero and styles","/docs/custom-code",[94,97,100],{"id":95,"text":96},"a-custom-hero","A custom hero",{"id":98,"text":99},"custom-styles","Custom styles",{"id":101,"text":102},"everything-else","Everything else",{"title":104,"path":105,"headings":106},"Deploying","/docs/deploying",[107,110,113,116],{"id":108,"text":109},"what-it-does","What it does",{"id":111,"text":112},"your-own-domain","Your own domain",{"id":114,"text":115},"taking-a-site-down","Taking a site down",{"id":117,"text":118},"somewhere-else","Somewhere else",{"title":120,"path":121,"headings":122},"Updating a site","/docs/updating",[123,126,129,132],{"id":124,"text":125},"run-it","Run it",{"id":127,"text":128},"what-it-changes","What it changes",{"id":130,"text":131},"what-it-leaves-alone","What it leaves alone",{"id":133,"text":134},"where-the-template-comes-from","Where the template comes from",{"label":136,"items":137},"Reference",[138,148],{"title":139,"path":140,"headings":141},"Agents","/docs/agents",[142,145],{"id":143,"text":144},"having-an-agent-build-the-site","Having an agent build the site",{"id":146,"text":147},"reading-a-published-site","Reading a published site",{"title":149,"path":150,"headings":151},"Limits","/docs/limits",[152,155,158,161],{"id":153,"text":154},"two-tools-on-one-site","Two tools on one site",{"id":156,"text":157},"dns-only-on-cloudflare","DNS only on Cloudflare",{"id":159,"text":160},"github-pages-needs-a-public-repository","GitHub Pages needs a public repository",{"id":162,"text":163},"template-code-is-the-templates","Template code is the template's"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"doc":1,"prev":7,"next":10},{"title":2,"description":3,"html":4,"path":5,"group":6},"Deploying","Publishing to GitHub Pages, and using your own domain.","\u003Cp class=\"lead\">\u003Ccode>scripts/deploy-pages.sh\u003C/code> builds the site and publishes it to GitHub Pages. Run it again whenever you change something.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"what-it-does\">What it does\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-it-does\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Col>\n\u003Cli>Stops if \u003Ccode>site.config.ts\u003C/code> still has a \u003Ccode>TODO:\u003C/code> in it.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Creates a public GitHub repository for the site, named after its folder, if there isn&#39;t one.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Pushes \u003Ccode>main\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Builds the site for the address in \u003Ccode>origin\u003C/code>.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Replaces the \u003Ccode>gh-pages\u003C/code> branch with the build and turns on Pages.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ol>\n\u003Cp>Pages needs a public repository on a free GitHub plan. The site&#39;s repository is separate from your tool&#39;s, so the tool can stay private.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"your-own-domain\">Your own domain\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#your-own-domain\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>Set \u003Ccode>origin\u003C/code> in \u003Ccode>site.config.ts\u003C/code> to the address, like \u003Ccode>https://mytool.example.com\u003C/code>, and deploy. The script sees the domain isn&#39;t on github.io, so it builds without a subfolder, adds the \u003Ccode>CNAME\u003C/code> file and tells GitHub about the domain.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>If the domain&#39;s DNS is on Cloudflare, the script adds the DNS record too. It needs a Cloudflare token for that, which you save once per Mac:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"code edge\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki css-variables\" style=\"background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--shiki-token-function)\">scripts/cloudflare-token.sh\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"copy\" aria-label=\"Copy code\">\u003Csvg class=\"idle\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Crect x=\"5.5\" y=\"5.5\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M10.5 3.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5H4A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 2.5 3.5V9A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 4 10.5\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003Csvg class=\"done\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"m3.5 8.5 3 3 6-7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/button>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>It opens Cloudflare&#39;s token page, checks the token you paste, and keeps it in your login keychain. From then on every deploy makes sure there&#39;s a DNS-only \u003Ccode>CNAME\u003C/code> from the domain to your \u003Ccode>github.io\u003C/code> address. It never replaces a record that points somewhere else. It tells you what&#39;s there and stops.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Without a token, add that \u003Ccode>CNAME\u003C/code> yourself. Leave Cloudflare&#39;s proxy off for it, so GitHub can issue the certificate. HTTPS usually works within a few minutes, and the next deploy switches on HTTPS only.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"taking-a-site-down\">Taking a site down\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#taking-a-site-down\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"code edge\">\u003Cpre class=\"shiki css-variables\" style=\"background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--shiki-token-function)\">scripts/remove-site.sh\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--shiki-token-string)\"> --yes\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"copy\" aria-label=\"Copy code\">\u003Csvg class=\"idle\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Crect x=\"5.5\" y=\"5.5\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" rx=\"2\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M10.5 3.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5H4A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 2.5 3.5V9A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 4 10.5\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003Csvg class=\"done\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"m3.5 8.5 3 3 6-7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/button>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>It stops GitHub Pages serving the site, deletes its Cloudflare DNS record if it points at GitHub, and archives the repository. The archive keeps everything, read-only, so you can bring it back later.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"somewhere-else\">Somewhere else\u003Ca class=\"anchor\" href=\"#somewhere-else\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">\u003Csvg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\u003Cpath d=\"M6.5 9.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 0l2.2-2.2a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4-4l-.7.7\"/>\u003Cpath d=\"M9.5 6.5a2.8 2.8 0 0 0-4 0L3.3 8.7a2.8 2.8 0 0 0 4 4l.7-.7\"/>\u003C/svg>\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>npm run build\u003C/code> writes a plain static site to \u003Ccode>build/\u003C/code>. Any static host can serve it. Set \u003Ccode>VITE_ORIGIN\u003C/code> to the address, and \u003Ccode>VITE_BASE\u003C/code> too if it lives under a subfolder.\u003C/p>\n","/docs/deploying","Guide",{"title":8,"path":9},"Custom hero and styles","/docs/custom-code",{"title":11,"path":12},"Updating a site","/docs/updating"],"uses":{"params":["page"]}}]}
